@startuml StripeWebhook Sequence

title Stripe Webhook API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

box "External" #F8FAFC
    participant "Stripe" as stripe
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "t_payment" as t_payment
    database "t_order" as t_order
    database "t_order_item" as t_order_item
    database "t_shop_product_sku_lot" as t_shop_product_sku_lot
    database "m_campaign_budget_ledger" as m_campaign_budget_ledger
    database "m_campaign_budget" as m_campaign_budget
end box

stripe -> api: POST v1/payment/webhook/stripe (raw body and stripe-signature)
activate stripe
    activate api
        api -> app: [**StripeWebhookCommandHandler**] Process request
        activate app
            app -> app: Create request context; generate requestId when omitted
            app -> domain: Verify stripe-signature against the raw body with the signing secret; the timestamp is within 5 minutes and the body is JSON
            activate domain
            domain -> app: Valid or invalid
            deactivate domain
            alt Signature missing or wrong, body is not JSON, or timestamp is too old
                app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
                api -> stripe: Bad request; nothing is changed
            else Valid event
                app -> app: Read the event type and its data (providerPaymentId, chargeId, eventAt, paymentName, failure, refundId)
                alt The event type is not handled
                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action IGNORED
                    api -> stripe: Event received
                else The event type is handled
                    note over app, infra
                        - The payment is found by `provider_payment_id` (the PaymentIntent id) and then the order of the payment is locked (`FOR UPDATE`). The lock order is always the order first, the same as the start payment, the refund and the shipping APIs, so they never wait for each other in a circle, and every update of the payment is guarded by its status. Every event is applied by the state of the payment, so the same event twice gives the same result (idempotent) and events that arrive in another order never move a final payment back:
                          PENDING / payment_intent.processing / PROCESSING / no change / PAYMENT_PROCESSING
                          PENDING / payment_intent.succeeded / COMPLETED / WAIT_PAYMENT -> PAYMENT_CONFIRMED (not WAIT_PAYMENT: a late payment, see below) / PAYMENT_COMPLETED
                          PROCESSING / payment_intent.succeeded / COMPLETED / WAIT_PAYMENT -> PAYMENT_CONFIRMED (not WAIT_PAYMENT: a late payment, see below) / PAYMENT_COMPLETED
                          PENDING / payment_intent.payment_failed / FAILED (failure_code, failure_message) / no change (still WAIT_PAYMENT, the customer can try again) / PAYMENT_FAILED
                          PROCESSING / payment_intent.payment_failed / FAILED / no change / PAYMENT_FAILED
                          PENDING / payment_intent.canceled / CANCELLED / no change / PAYMENT_CANCELLED
                          COMPLETED / charge.refunded / REFUNDED / PAYMENT_CONFIRMED -> REFUNDED and the stock goes back to the lots / PAYMENT_REFUNDED
                          FAILED, CANCELLED / payment_intent.succeeded / REFUNDED (late payment, see below) / no change / LATE_PAYMENT_REFUNDED
                          any other / any other / no change / no change / IGNORED
                        - On `payment_intent.succeeded` the payment gets `transaction_code` (the charge id), `transaction_at` (the time of the event, UTC) and `payment_name` (a
                          label such as `Visa 4242` or `PromptPay`), and the order is changed with a guarded update (`AND status = 'WAIT_PAYMENT'`). The order is accepted
                          even when `expires_at` has passed as long as the order is still `WAIT_PAYMENT`, because the stock is still held.
                        - **Late payment:** when the guarded update of the order changes no row (the order was cancelled or expired first), or the payment is already FAILED or
                          CANCELLED, the money must not stay with the platform. The system asks Stripe for a full refund (`Idempotency-Key` = `refund-` + payment id) and sets
                          the payment to REFUNDED directly with `refund_reason` = `Late payment: the order is not waiting for payment`. The order is not changed and the stock
                          is not given back again.
                        - On `charge.refunded` (a refund made in the Stripe dashboard or by the refund API) a COMPLETED payment becomes REFUNDED. When the order is
                          `PAYMENT_CONFIRMED` it becomes `REFUNDED` and the quantity of every item goes back to its lot, otherwise (the order has started to ship) only the
                          payment changes and the event is written to the log for a person to handle.
                        - When `charge.refunded` turns a COMPLETED payment into REFUNDED the budget that the order took from a campaign goes back in the same transaction as the
                          stock (C7 and C9, approved by the product owner on 2026-11-06), with the same `RELEASE`
                          ledger rows as the refund API. A refund that arrives after the order was already cancelled (the late payment rule above) does not touch the budget,
                          it went back when the order was cancelled.
                        - The webhook also makes the database match when another API called Stripe and its `COMMIT` failed afterwards (approved by the product owner on
                          2026-11-08): a `charge.refunded` after a refund of `05-refund-payment` finds the payment COMPLETED and applies the refund (payment and order
                          REFUNDED, the stock and the budget go back, the lots in `lot_id` order), and a `payment_intent.canceled` after a cancel of `sales/05` or after a
                          replaced payment of `01-start-payment` finds the payment PENDING and sets it CANCELLED. The refund of a late payment uses the `Idempotency-Key`
                          `refund-<paymentId>`, so the retry of an event that failed after Stripe answered refunds once.
                    end note
                    app -> infra: BEGIN READ COMMITTED
                    activate infra
                    alt Work completes before commit
                        app -> infra: QUERY - Get the payment of the event
                        infra -> t_payment: QUERY - Get the payment of the event
                        activate t_payment
                            note right of t_payment
                                SELECT
                                    p.id as payment_id,
                                    p.order_id,
                                    p.status,
                                    p.payment_method,
                                    p.amount
                                FROM payment.t_payment p
                                WHERE p.provider_payment_id = '<sequence.providerPaymentId>' -- the PaymentIntent id of the event, no row means the event is IGNORED
                                AND p.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                            end note
                            t_payment -> infra: Return query result
                        deactivate t_payment
                        infra -> app: Return the payment or no row
                        alt No payment has this PaymentIntent id
                            app -> infra: COMMIT
                            app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action IGNORED
                            api -> stripe: Event received
                        else Payment found
                            app -> infra: QUERY - Get the order of the payment and lock it
                            infra -> t_order: QUERY - Get the order of the payment and lock it
                            activate t_order
                                note right of t_order
                                    SELECT
                                        o.id as order_id,
                                        o.status
                                    FROM sales.t_order o
                                    WHERE o.id = '<sequence.orderId>'
                                    FOR UPDATE -- taken before any update of the payment
                                end note
                                t_order -> infra: Return query result
                            deactivate t_order
                            infra -> app: Return the locked order
                            alt PENDING and payment_intent.processing
                                app -> infra: UPDATE - Mark the payment as processing
                                infra -> t_payment: UPDATE - Mark the payment as processing
                                activate t_payment
                                    note right of t_payment
                                        UPDATE payment.t_payment
                                        SET
                                            updated_by = 'system',
                                            updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                            status = 'PROCESSING'
                                        WHERE id = '<sequence.paymentId>'
                                        AND status = 'PENDING'
                                        RETURNING id as payment_id, status
                                    end note
                                    t_payment -> infra: Return updated result
                                deactivate t_payment
                                infra -> app: Return the processing payment or no row
                                alt A row changed
                                    app -> infra: COMMIT
                                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action PAYMENT_PROCESSING
                                    api -> stripe: Event received
                                else Nothing changed: the payment changed in the meantime
                                    app -> infra: COMMIT
                                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action IGNORED
                                    api -> stripe: Event received
                                end
                            else PENDING or PROCESSING and payment_intent.succeeded
                                app -> infra: UPDATE - Mark the payment as completed
                                infra -> t_payment: UPDATE - Mark the payment as completed
                                activate t_payment
                                    note right of t_payment
                                        UPDATE payment.t_payment
                                        SET
                                            updated_by = 'system',
                                            updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                            status = 'COMPLETED',
                                            transaction_code = '<sequence.chargeId>',
                                            transaction_at = '<sequence.eventAt>', -- the time of the event in UTC
                                            payment_name = '<sequence.paymentName>'
                                        WHERE id = '<sequence.paymentId>'
                                        AND status IN ('PENDING', 'PROCESSING') -- another status means the event is IGNORED or a late payment
                                        RETURNING id as payment_id, status
                                    end note
                                    t_payment -> infra: Return updated result
                                deactivate t_payment
                                infra -> app: Return the completed payment or no row
                                alt A row changed
                                    app -> infra: UPDATE - Confirm the order
                                    infra -> t_order: UPDATE - Confirm the order
                                    activate t_order
                                        note right of t_order
                                            UPDATE sales.t_order
                                            SET
                                                updated_by = 'system',
                                                updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                                status = 'PAYMENT_CONFIRMED'
                                            WHERE id = '<sequence.orderId>'
                                            AND status = 'WAIT_PAYMENT' -- no row changed means a late payment, the money is refunded
                                            RETURNING id as order_id, status
                                        end note
                                        t_order -> infra: Return updated result
                                    deactivate t_order
                                    infra -> app: Return the confirmed order or no row
                                    alt A row changed: the order was WAIT_PAYMENT
                                        app -> infra: COMMIT
                                        app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action PAYMENT_COMPLETED
                                        api -> stripe: Event received
                                    else No row changed: the order was cancelled or expired first (late payment)
                                        app -> stripe: Ask for a full refund (Idempotency-Key = refund-<paymentId>)
                                        stripe -> app: Return refundId
                                        app -> infra: UPDATE - Mark the payment as refunded
                                        infra -> t_payment: UPDATE - Mark the payment as refunded
                                        activate t_payment
                                            note right of t_payment
                                                UPDATE payment.t_payment
                                                SET
                                                    updated_by = 'system',
                                                    updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                                    status = 'REFUNDED',
                                                    transaction_code = COALESCE(transaction_code, '<sequence.chargeId>'),
                                                    transaction_at = COALESCE(transaction_at, '<sequence.eventAt>'),
                                                    provider_refund_id = '<sequence.refundId>',
                                                    refunded_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                                    refund_reason = '<sequence.refundReason>' -- 'Late payment: the order is not waiting for payment' for a late payment
                                                WHERE id = '<sequence.paymentId>'
                                                AND status IN ('COMPLETED', 'FAILED', 'CANCELLED') -- COMPLETED for charge.refunded, FAILED and CANCELLED for a late payment
                                                RETURNING id as payment_id, status
                                            end note
                                            t_payment -> infra: Return updated result
                                        deactivate t_payment
                                        infra -> app: Return the refunded payment
                                        app -> infra: COMMIT
                                        app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action LATE_PAYMENT_REFUNDED
                                        api -> stripe: Event received
                                    end
                                else Nothing changed: the payment changed in the meantime
                                    app -> infra: COMMIT
                                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action IGNORED
                                    api -> stripe: Event received
                                end
                            else FAILED or CANCELLED and payment_intent.succeeded (late payment)
                                app -> stripe: Ask for a full refund (Idempotency-Key = refund-<paymentId>)
                                stripe -> app: Return refundId
                                app -> infra: UPDATE - Mark the payment as refunded
                                infra -> t_payment: UPDATE - Mark the payment as refunded
                                activate t_payment
                                    note right of t_payment
                                        UPDATE payment.t_payment
                                        SET
                                            updated_by = 'system',
                                            updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                            status = 'REFUNDED',
                                            transaction_code = COALESCE(transaction_code, '<sequence.chargeId>'),
                                            transaction_at = COALESCE(transaction_at, '<sequence.eventAt>'),
                                            provider_refund_id = '<sequence.refundId>',
                                            refunded_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                            refund_reason = '<sequence.refundReason>' -- 'Late payment: the order is not waiting for payment' for a late payment
                                        WHERE id = '<sequence.paymentId>'
                                        AND status IN ('COMPLETED', 'FAILED', 'CANCELLED') -- COMPLETED for charge.refunded, FAILED and CANCELLED for a late payment
                                        RETURNING id as payment_id, status
                                    end note
                                    t_payment -> infra: Return updated result
                                deactivate t_payment
                                infra -> app: Return the refunded payment
                                app -> infra: COMMIT
                                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action LATE_PAYMENT_REFUNDED
                                api -> stripe: Event received
                            else PENDING or PROCESSING and payment_intent.payment_failed
                                app -> infra: UPDATE - Mark the payment as failed
                                infra -> t_payment: UPDATE - Mark the payment as failed
                                activate t_payment
                                    note right of t_payment
                                        UPDATE payment.t_payment
                                        SET
                                            updated_by = 'system',
                                            updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                            status = 'FAILED',
                                            failure_code = '<sequence.failureCode>',
                                            failure_message = '<sequence.failureMessage>'
                                        WHERE id = '<sequence.paymentId>'
                                        AND status IN ('PENDING', 'PROCESSING')
                                        RETURNING id as payment_id, status
                                    end note
                                    t_payment -> infra: Return updated result
                                deactivate t_payment
                                infra -> app: Return the failed payment or no row
                                alt A row changed
                                    app -> infra: COMMIT
                                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action PAYMENT_FAILED
                                    api -> stripe: Event received
                                else Nothing changed: the payment changed in the meantime
                                    app -> infra: COMMIT
                                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action IGNORED
                                    api -> stripe: Event received
                                end
                            else PENDING and payment_intent.canceled
                                app -> infra: UPDATE - Mark the payment as cancelled
                                infra -> t_payment: UPDATE - Mark the payment as cancelled
                                activate t_payment
                                    note right of t_payment
                                        UPDATE payment.t_payment
                                        SET
                                            updated_by = 'system',
                                            updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                            status = 'CANCELLED'
                                        WHERE id = '<sequence.paymentId>'
                                        AND status = 'PENDING'
                                        RETURNING id as payment_id, status
                                    end note
                                    t_payment -> infra: Return updated result
                                deactivate t_payment
                                infra -> app: Return the cancelled payment or no row
                                alt A row changed
                                    app -> infra: COMMIT
                                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action PAYMENT_CANCELLED
                                    api -> stripe: Event received
                                else Nothing changed: the payment changed in the meantime
                                    app -> infra: COMMIT
                                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action IGNORED
                                    api -> stripe: Event received
                                end
                            else COMPLETED and charge.refunded
                                app -> infra: UPDATE - Mark the payment as refunded
                                infra -> t_payment: UPDATE - Mark the payment as refunded
                                activate t_payment
                                    note right of t_payment
                                        UPDATE payment.t_payment
                                        SET
                                            updated_by = 'system',
                                            updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                            status = 'REFUNDED',
                                            transaction_code = COALESCE(transaction_code, '<sequence.chargeId>'),
                                            transaction_at = COALESCE(transaction_at, '<sequence.eventAt>'),
                                            provider_refund_id = '<sequence.refundId>',
                                            refunded_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                            refund_reason = '<sequence.refundReason>' -- 'Late payment: the order is not waiting for payment' for a late payment
                                        WHERE id = '<sequence.paymentId>'
                                        AND status IN ('COMPLETED', 'FAILED', 'CANCELLED') -- COMPLETED for charge.refunded, FAILED and CANCELLED for a late payment
                                        RETURNING id as payment_id, status
                                    end note
                                    t_payment -> infra: Return updated result
                                deactivate t_payment
                                infra -> app: Return the refunded payment or no row
                                alt A row changed
                                    app -> infra: UPDATE - Refund the order
                                    infra -> t_order: UPDATE - Refund the order
                                    activate t_order
                                        note right of t_order
                                            UPDATE sales.t_order
                                            SET
                                                updated_by = 'system',
                                                updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                                status = 'REFUNDED'
                                            WHERE id = '<sequence.orderId>'
                                            AND status = 'PAYMENT_CONFIRMED' -- no row changed means the order has started to ship, only the payment changes
                                            RETURNING id as order_id, status
                                        end note
                                        t_order -> infra: Return updated result
                                    deactivate t_order
                                    infra -> app: Return the refunded order or no row
                                    alt A row changed: the order was PAYMENT_CONFIRMED
                                        app -> infra: QUERY - Get the items of the refunded order
                                        infra -> t_order_item: QUERY - Get the items of the refunded order
                                        activate t_order_item
                                            note right of t_order_item
                                                SELECT
                                                    oi.id as order_item_id,
                                                    oi.lot_id,
                                                    oi.quantity
                                                FROM sales.t_order_item oi
                                                WHERE oi.order_id = '<sequence.orderId>'
                                                AND oi.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                                ORDER BY oi.lot_id -- the lots are locked in id order, the same as the checkout
                                            end note
                                            t_order_item -> infra: Return query result
                                        deactivate t_order_item
                                        infra -> app: Return the items with their lots and quantities
                                        loop For every item in lot id order
                                            app -> infra: UPDATE - Give the quantity back to the lot
                                            infra -> t_shop_product_sku_lot: UPDATE - Give the quantity back to the lot
                                            activate t_shop_product_sku_lot
                                                note right of t_shop_product_sku_lot
                                                    UPDATE shop.t_shop_product_sku_lot
                                                    SET
                                                        updated_by = 'system',
                                                        updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                                        quantity = quantity + '<sequence.quantity>' -- the lot may be DELETED or ARCHIVED, it still gets the quantity back
                                                    WHERE id = '<sequence.lotId>'
                                                    RETURNING id as lot_id, quantity
                                                end note
                                                t_shop_product_sku_lot -> infra: Return updated result
                                            deactivate t_shop_product_sku_lot
                                            infra -> app: Return the lot and its quantity
                                        end
                                        app -> infra: QUERY - Get the budget that the order took
                                        infra -> m_campaign_budget_ledger: QUERY - Get the budget that the order took
                                        activate m_campaign_budget_ledger
                                            note right of m_campaign_budget_ledger
                                                SELECT
                                                    l.campaign_budget_id,
                                                    l.campaign_id,
                                                    l.usage,
                                                    l.reference
                                                FROM campaign.m_campaign_budget_ledger l
                                                WHERE l.order_id = '<sequence.orderId>'
                                                AND l.entry_type = 'RESERVE'
                                                AND NOT EXISTS (
                                                    SELECT 1
                                                    FROM campaign.m_campaign_budget_ledger r
                                                    WHERE r.order_id = l.order_id
                                                    AND r.campaign_budget_id = l.campaign_budget_id
                                                    AND r.entry_type = 'RELEASE'
                                                ) -- a budget that was already given back is skipped, so nothing goes back twice
                                                ORDER BY l.campaign_budget_id
                                            end note
                                            m_campaign_budget_ledger -> infra: Return query result
                                        deactivate m_campaign_budget_ledger
                                        infra -> app: Return the RESERVE rows that are not released yet
                                        loop For every budget in budget id order
                                            app -> infra: INSERT - Write the release in the ledger
                                            infra -> m_campaign_budget_ledger: INSERT - Write the release in the ledger
                                            activate m_campaign_budget_ledger
                                                note right of m_campaign_budget_ledger
                                                    INSERT INTO campaign.m_campaign_budget_ledger (created_by, campaign_budget_id, campaign_id, order_id, entry_type, reference, usage, remaining)
                                                    VALUES ('system', '<sequence.campaignBudgetId>', '<sequence.campaignId>', '<sequence.orderId>', 'RELEASE', '<sequence.reference>', '<sequence.usage>', '<sequence.remaining>')
                                                    RETURNING id as ledger_id
                                                end note
                                                m_campaign_budget_ledger -> infra: Return inserted result
                                            deactivate m_campaign_budget_ledger
                                            infra -> app: Return ledger_id
                                            app -> infra: UPDATE - Give the budget back
                                            infra -> m_campaign_budget: UPDATE - Give the budget back
                                            activate m_campaign_budget
                                                note right of m_campaign_budget
                                                    UPDATE campaign.m_campaign_budget
                                                    SET
                                                        updated_by = 'system',
                                                        updated_at = NOW() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC',
                                                        remaining = remaining + '<sequence.usage>' -- the budget may be INACTIVE, LOCKED or ARCHIVED by now, it still gets the amount back
                                                    WHERE id = '<sequence.campaignBudgetId>'
                                                    RETURNING id as budget_id, remaining
                                                end note
                                                m_campaign_budget -> infra: Return updated result
                                            deactivate m_campaign_budget
                                            infra -> app: Return the budget and what is left
                                        end
                                        app -> infra: COMMIT
                                        app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action PAYMENT_REFUNDED
                                        api -> stripe: Event received
                                    else No row changed: the order has started to ship, only the payment changes
                                        app -> app: Write the event to the log for a person to handle
                                        app -> infra: COMMIT
                                        app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action PAYMENT_REFUNDED
                                        api -> stripe: Event received
                                    end
                                else Nothing changed: the payment changed in the meantime
                                    app -> infra: COMMIT
                                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action IGNORED
                                    api -> stripe: Event received
                                end
                            else Any other status and event
                                app -> infra: COMMIT
                                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 action IGNORED
                                api -> stripe: Event received
                            end
                        end
                    else Timeout before COMMIT
                        note over app, infra
                            A timeout can interrupt any preceding SQL or domain step.
                            No success response is sent without a successful COMMIT.
                        end note
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
                        api -> stripe: Request timeout
                    else Unexpected failure before COMMIT
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 500 generic error; no new bizCode
                        api -> stripe: Internal server error
                    end
                    deactivate infra
                end
            end
        deactivate app
    deactivate api
deactivate stripe

@enduml
